  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 119 PM CDT Thu May 28 2026\n\nHigh pressure will lead to dry and warm conditions through early \nnext week. Highs from the mid-80s to the mid-90s with heat index \nvalues around 100-105 will lead to minor to moderate heat-related \nimpacts. Those who are sensitive to the heat and those who work \noutside should take breaks in the shade and drink plenty of water.\n\nRain will return again Monday night/Tuesday as the ridge weakens a \nbit and shortwaves begin to creep into the area and interact with \nthe seabreeze. Chances are low to medium (20-50%) through the end of \nthe work week.\n\nWave periods will increase to around 8 seconds as we head into the \nweekend, which could be enough to lead to minor coastal flooding. \nFor now, it appears that tidal values will be low enough to keep \nwater from reaching the dunes, but this will need to be monitored \nclosely.",
